# WHAT IT COVERS: the 2026-10-25 stream, 132.6 minutes cut to the gameplay its video shows, the
# longest stream here, captured through NvFBC on the defaults with the blends drawn by the pan
# shader (-blend pan), which changes how a blend looks and nothing the replay models. The policy
# is the one the tree ships. The game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 812 times (367 an hour) and stalled
# for 100 ms or more 177 times (80 an hour), in 212 bursts, 95 of them with a stall, and with no
# periodic stretch. The lock released 9 times in the field: 473.62, 1734.13, 3754.70, 4410.23,
# 4416.45, 4456.18, 4808.01, 7516.86 and 7762.46 s. The replay releases at the same moments
# except 473.62 s (8 presents after a field move onto a phase step) and 7762.46 s (at the end of
# a 4-present blend run). The worst blend run, 34 presents in the field and on the replay, is at
# 4807.96 s, beside the 4808.01 s release. Of the 89 moves on the replay, 17 land more than 2 ms
# from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 50.218 s, from the 2419
# marked frames in its first 40 s, within 0.38 ms of that offset (p90). The video runs 7955.3 s
# with no holes, opens on gameplay (a still view over the town, marked) and ends on gameplay
# indoors after the sleep wheel and the inventory, so the cut is the whole video, 50.2 s to
# 8005.5 s of log time, and the marked frames lie inside it. Inside the cut, 57 seconds in 51 runs
# fall out of the 60 fps regime. One is longer than 2 s: 6615 s to 6617 s, the inventory opening
# and closing, left in. The rest are single hitch seconds, or two in a row.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line (the plain arm) reads synth 0.8% against 0.8%, worst run 34 against 34, runs >= 50
# 0 against 0 and pull wraps 139 against 133. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran and
# what the counts here use, blends are 3662 against 3651, repeats 1437 against 1445, skips 457
# against 456, pull wraps 61.1 an hour against 60.2 and the worst run 34 against 34, all inside
# the corpus's fidelity limits. The replay makes 89 moves, 18 of them late, and the field's log
# has 95 in the window; it releases the lock 7 times against the field's 9 (above).
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
